redfin 1255: Touch ID match before wake (kern.sweet_mesa_wake bit 3), kern.sweet_mesa_prematch_ms

The owner's screen-off unlock order: with the display off a finger wakes the phone only when it matches. Bit 3
(use kern.sweet_mesa_wake=12): a FINGER_DOWN while dark presses nothing; sweetfpcd (ws-fpcd-e, WAKEDET {1,
FPCD_WD_PREMATCH}) identifies the touch and sends FPCD_EV_PREMATCH (14) or FPCD_EV_PREMATCH_NOMATCH (15).
A pre-match passing the match gate (kern.sweet_mesa_match 2, or 1 + verified HAT) and sweet_pc_bio_allowed is
stored (kern.sweet_mesa_prematch_ms, default 2000, single use) and the power button pressed; the next 4 MatchMode
(not extend) takes it (sweetfpcd gets FPCD_MM_PREMATCHED and does not identify that touch again) and 30 ms later a
thread call sends FingerOn + the stored match through fpcd_translate (keybag / ACM / unlock delay rules, record),
FingerOff if the finger was lifted. Touch ID not allowed (lockout, passcode after restart / 48 h, backoff): the
press comes without a stored match (passcode screen). A wrong finger: a failed attempt under the 1225 rules, no
wake. A touch that began within kern.sweet_mesa_wake_ms of display off never wakes. Bit 0 (1235 wake on any finger)
stays selectable (5). boot-arg sweettouchid bit 3: kern.sweet_mesa_wake 12. Default 0: nothing changes.

